// Policy: 16_deploy_requires_recent_tests   (Dogwood temporal policy)
// Category: Stateful control (Chapter 3, Section 3.7)
// Intent: Grant a production deploy only if run_tests completed successfully
//         in the same policy session within the last five minutes.
//
// Pair with a plain permit for ci___run_tests: an action is recorded as a
//   ::response event only if some policy allowed it. Strict validation may
//   reject that plain permit as "Overly Permissive"; the author created it
//   with --validation-mode IGNORE_ALL_FINDINGS and kept strict validation on
//   the temporal policy (2026-10-12 lab).
// Serialize in the client: the ::response event exists only after
//   run_tests finishes. In the same lab, sending both calls in parallel got
//   the deploy denied 98 of 100 times; sending deploy after the response
//   arrived, 0 of 600. A Strands agent issued both in the same turn in all
//   10 sessions.
// Policy 09 still applies (forbid outside business hours).

permit (
  principal,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"devops-prod___deploy",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:REGION:ACCOUNT:gateway/GATEWAY_ID"
)
when temporal {
  formerly within 5m AgentCore::Action::"ci___run_tests"::response{
    eventResource: resource
  }
};
